    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91649.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Exactly. It was funny. I was in a grocery store in Maine and I I couldn't find any yeast. I was going to make some waffles. that you mix up the night before with yeast. And I said to one of those store clerks, I said, you always have tons of yeast. And they told me that there'd been a real run on yeast because people were baking not only sourdough, but all sorts of kinds of where you have to have a starter, but all sorts of kinds of breads.",
