    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Well, I grew up in Caribou, as you know, and so I was used to traveling around Arista County and traveling to Bangor after the potato harvest with my family. I remember going through the Hanesville Woods before I-95 was all the way to Holton. So I've seen the difference that good roads can make to our state. And I think that I'm especially attuned to that, having grown up in northern Maine, where it's more rural, where people have to travel longer distances than people who are living in the southern part of the state.",
