  {
    "episode_id": 91649,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91649.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "unfortunately nowadays, girls know that you can be whatever you want to be, and so can boys. I think that's still an important message to say. One reason I visited more than 200 schools in the state of Maine is I want those little girls and little boys who are growing up in small communities in rural Maine to know that they can grow up to be a United States senator or president or whatever they want to be. A doctor, a lawyer, a school teacher, a scientist, whatever, a constructor of good roads and bridges, whatever it is, someone who creates jobs forever. for others. So that's the message that I wanted to give. I know this is a hard time to be going to school because it's so disruptive, but we've got to make the best of it. Unfortunately, we have really dedicated teachers in Maine who are determined to ensure that their students are not left behind.",
